	<annotations>
		<text id="0" type="text/markdown" rect="(30, 10, 420, 50)" font-family="Helvetica" font-size="14">**Lab 3: Correlations and Hypothesis Testing**  
Housing dataset, 506 towns</text>
		<text id="1" type="text/markdown" rect="(540, 40, 240, 70)" font-family="Helvetica" font-size="14">**Step 1: Initial Data Exploration**  
Table, box plot and distribution of the raw data.</text>
		<text id="2" type="text/markdown" rect="(20, 610, 150, 110)" font-family="Helvetica" font-size="14">**Step 2: Select Columns**  
MEDV moved from target to a feature.</text>
		<text id="3" type="text/markdown" rect="(800, 550, 240, 80)" font-family="Helvetica" font-size="14">**Steps 3-4: Correlations**  
Pearson correlations with MEDV and the scatter plot of the chosen pair.</text>
		<text id="4" type="text/markdown" rect="(800, 800, 290, 80)" font-family="Helvetica" font-size="14">**Step 5: Formula**  
log2 of the feature most correlated to MEDV, then correlations and scatter plot again.</text>
		<text id="5" type="text/markdown" rect="(1100, 330, 240, 100)" font-family="Helvetica" font-size="14">**Steps 6-7: Discretize CRIM**  
CRIM split into 2 equal-frequency groups, then MEDV compared between them.</text>
		<text id="6" type="text/markdown" rect="(640, 900, 280, 80)" font-family="Helvetica" font-size="14">**Step 8: Discretize RM**  
RM split into 2 equal-frequency groups, then every attribute tested.</text>
		<arrow id="7" start="(540, 60)" end="(455, 78)" fill="#C1272D" />
		<arrow id="8" start="(540, 90)" end="(455, 170)" fill="#C1272D" />
		<arrow id="9" start="(550, 110)" end="(455, 265)" fill="#C1272D" />
